# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3D Code World (demo version) — optional environment variables
# Copy to .env.local to override. Only VITE_* variables reach the browser.
# This demo has no backend: progress is stored in the learner's browser.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Python runner used by the editor's "Run" button:
#   pyodide  – CPython compiled to WebAssembly, executed in a sandboxed iframe + Web Worker
#              in the learner's browser (~10 MB, downloaded once and cached by the browser)
#   disabled – Python execution switched off (the editor explains why)
VITE_PYTHON_RUNNER=pyodide

# Where the Pyodide runtime is served from.
# Default: self-hosted copy placed in public/pyodide/ by `npm install` (scripts/copy-pyodide.mjs).
# Alternative CDN: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/pyodide/v0.26.4/full/
# Cross-origin note: the sandbox iframe has an opaque origin, so this location must send
# `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` (see public/_headers and vercel.json).
VITE_PYODIDE_BASE_URL=/pyodide/v0.26.4/
